{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_8563ee70-9bac-42c9-abae-d77f23efafe","tool_call":{"semSearchToolCall":{"args":{"query":"User Story 4 merge condition checker auto merge implementation","targetDirectories":[],"explanation":""},"result":{"success":{"results":"<search_result path=\"specs/001-github-agent-automation/data-model.md\" startLine=\"345\" endLine=\"393\">\n   345|- Send Discord notification (embed with error history)\n   346|- Stop auto-retry loop\n   347|- Manual re-trigger available via CLI with `--reset-count` flag\n   348|\n   349|### PullRequest Merge Conditions (Definition of Done)\n   350|\n   351|A PR can be auto-merged when ALL of the following are true:\n   352|\n   353|1. **CI Success**: All CIStatus records have conclusion=success\n   354|2. **Codex Approval**: At least one ReviewFeedback has approval_detected=true\n   355|3. **No Conflicts**: PullRequest.mergeable=true (from GitHub API)\n   356|4. **Status**: PullRequest.status=open\n   357|\n   358|**Checking Strategy**:\n   359|- Re-evaluate on every check_suite.completed webhook\n   360|- Re-evaluate on every Codex review comment webhook\n   361|- Use MergeConditionChecker service to validate all conditions\n   362|- Call AutoMergeService if conditions met\n   363|\n   364|### BlockerGraph Dependencies\n   365|\n   366|**Dependency Resolution**:\n   367|- Task Y is blocked if EXISTS BlockerGraphEdges WHERE task_id=Y AND depends_on_task_id IN (open Issues)\n   368|- Task Y is unblocked when ALL dependencies have Issue.state=closed\n   369|- On Issue close: query BlockerGraphEdges to find newly unblocked tasks\n   370|- Trigger new AgentRun for each unblocked task\n   371|\n   372|**Cycle Detection**:\n   373|- Run DFS before starting execution\n   374|- If cycle detected: log warning, add to AuditLog, notify in GitHub comment\n   375|- Do NOT block execution (spec allows human resolution)\n   376|\n   377|## 制約情報（MySQL/GORM）\n   378|\n   379|### Unique Constraints\n   380|- Issue: UNIQUE(repo, number)\n   381|- PullRequest: UNIQUE(repo, number)\n   382|- AgentRun: UNIQUE(idempotency_key)\n   383|- CIStatus: UNIQUE(pr_id, check_suite_id, check_run_id)\n   384|- BlockerGraphEdges: PRIMARY KEY(task_id, depends_on_task_id)\n   385|\n   386|### Foreign Key Constraints\n   387|- AgentRun.issue_id → Issue.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n   388|- AgentRun.pr_id → PullRequest.id (ON DELETE SET NULL)\n   389|- PullRequest.issue_id → Issue.id (ON DELETE SET NULL)\n   390|- ReviewFeedback.pr_id → PullRequest.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n   391|- CIStatus.pr_id → PullRequest.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n   392|- BlockerGraphEdges.task_id → Issue.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n   393|- BlockerGraphEdges.depends_on_task_id → Issue.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n</search_result>\n<search_result path=\"specs/001-github-agent-automation/tasks.md\" startLine=\"199\" endLine=\"258\">\n   199|- [x] T096 [US3] Implement retry orchestrator managing retry_count (max 50) in internal/services/retry_orchestrator.go\n   200|- [x] T097 [US3] Create feedback aggregator combining review + CI results in internal/services/feedback_aggregator.go\n   201|- [x] T098 [US3] Implement K8s Job re-creation with aggregated feedback for AI retry in internal/services/kubernetes_job.go\n   202|- [x] T099 [US3] Add retry count validation and failure threshold (50) in internal/services/retry_orchestrator.go\n   203|- [x] T100 [US3] Implement failure notification to GitHub Issue on max retries in internal/services/github_notification.go\n   204|- [x] T101 [US3] Implement failure notification to Discord webhook on max retries in internal/services/discord_notification.go\n   205|- [x] T102 [US3] Add GitHub status comment updates for retry progress in internal/services/github_notification.go\n   206|- [x] T103 [US3] Store ReviewFeedback records for each review cycle in internal/repositories/review_feedback.go\n   207|\n   208|### Tests for User Story 3 (Test-First Development)\n   209|\n   210|- [ ] T104 [P] [US3] Write unit tests for CodexApprovalDetector (approval pattern matching)\n   211|- [ ] T105 [P] [US3] Write unit tests for RetryOrchestrator (max 50 retries logic)\n   212|- [ ] T106 [P] [US3] Write unit tests for FeedbackAggregator (review + CI combination)\n   213|- [ ] T107 [US3] Write integration test for CI failure → retry → success flow\n   214|\n   215|**Checkpoint**: All user stories 1-3 should now be independently functional - quality loop with automatic improvements\n   216|\n   217|---\n   218|\n   219|## Phase 6: User Story 4 - Approveと自動マージ (Priority: P2)\n   220|\n   221|**Goal**: PR が承認状態 (CI success + Codex approve + no conflicts) になったら自動でマージする\n   222|\n   223|**Independent Test**: PR に Approve を付与すると自動でマージされること\n   224|\n   225|### Implementation for User Story 4\n   226|\n   227|- [ ] T108 [P] [US4] Implement merge condition checker (CI + Codex + conflicts) in internal/services/merge_condition.go\n   228|- [ ] T109 [P] [US4] Create CI status aggregator from check_suite events in internal/services/ci_status_aggregator.go\n   229|- [ ] T110 [US4] Implement merge conflict detector via GitHub API in internal/services/merge_conflict_detector.go\n   230|- [ ] T111 [US4] Create auto-merge service with merge API call in internal/services/auto_merge.go\n   231|- [ ] T112 [US4] Implement webhook handler for status events (CI completion) in internal/webhooks/handlers/status.go\n   232|- [ ] T113 [US4] Add merge condition re-evaluation on Codex approval comment in internal/webhooks/handlers/pr_review_comment.go\n   233|- [ ] T114 [US4] Add merge condition re-evaluation on CI success in internal/webhooks/handlers/check_suite.go\n   234|- [ ] T115 [US4] Implement merge failure handling and notification in internal/services/auto_merge.go\n   235|- [ ] T116 [US4] Add GitHub status comment for merge success/failure in internal/services/github_notification.go\n   236|- [ ] T117 [US4] Add Discord notification for merge events in internal/services/discord_notification.go\n   237|\n   238|### Tests for User Story 4 (Test-First Development)\n   239|\n   240|- [ ] T118 [P] [US4] Write unit tests for MergeConditionChecker (DoD validation)\n   241|- [ ] T119 [P] [US4] Write unit tests for AutoMergeService (GitHub merge API call)\n   242|- [ ] T120 [US4] Write integration test for approve + CI success → auto-merge flow\n   243|\n   244|**Checkpoint**: All user stories 1-4 should now be independently functional - complete automation from comment to merge\n   245|\n   246|---\n   247|\n   248|## Phase 7: User Story 5 - ブロック解除によるタスク再開 (Priority: P3)\n   249|\n   250|**Goal**: 依存関係を持つタスクがブロックされている場合、完了によりブロックが解消されたタスクに自動着手する\n   251|\n   252|**Independent Test**: 依存関係グラフでブロック解除時に次タスク実行が開始されること\n   253|\n   254|### Implementation for User Story 5\n   255|\n   256|- [ ] T121 [P] [US5] Implement Issue blocker parser (\"blocked by\" / \"blocking\" syntax) in internal/services/issue_blocker_parser.go\n   257|- [ ] T122 [P] [US5] Create directed graph data structure for dependencies in internal/utils/dependency_graph.go\n   258|- [ ] T123 [US5] Implement blocker graph builder from Issue metadata in internal/services/blocker_graph.go\n</search_result>\n<search_result path=\"internal/clients/github.go\" startLine=\"380\" endLine=\"434\">\n   380|func (c *Client) MergePullRequest(ctx context.Context, owner, repo string, prNumber int, commitMessage string, mergeMethod string) (*github.PullRequestMergeResult, error) {\n   381|\tc.logger.Info(\"Merging GitHub pull request\",\n   382|\t\tzap.String(\"owner\", owner),\n   383|\t\tzap.String(\"repo\", repo),\n   384|\t\tzap.Int(\"pr_number\", prNumber),\n   385|\t\tzap.String(\"merge_method\", mergeMethod),\n   386|\t)\n   387|\n   388|\topts := &github.PullRequestOptions{\n   389|\t\tCommitTitle: commitMessage,\n   390|\t\tMergeMethod: mergeMethod,\n   391|\t}\n   392|\n   393|\tresult, resp, err := c.PullRequests.Merge(ctx, owner, repo, prNumber, commitMessage, opts)\n   394|\tif err != nil {\n   395|\t\treturn nil, c.handleError(err, resp, \"MergePullRequest\")\n   396|\t}\n   397|\n   398|\tc.handleRateLimit(resp)\n   399|\treturn result, nil\n   400|}\n   401|\n   402|// GetPullRequestMergeable checks if a pull request is mergeable\n   403|// Returns true if mergeable, false if not mergeable, error if status is unknown or error occurred\n   404|func (c *Client) GetPullRequestMergeable(ctx context.Context, owner, repo string, prNumber int) (bool, error) {\n   405|\tc.logger.Info(\"Checking GitHub pull request mergeable status\",\n   406|\t\tzap.String(\"owner\", owner),\n   407|\t\tzap.String(\"repo\", repo),\n   408|\t\tzap.Int(\"pr_number\", prNumber),\n   409|\t)\n   410|\n   411|\tpr, resp, err := c.PullRequests.Get(ctx, owner, repo, prNumber)\n   412|\tif err != nil {\n   413|\t\treturn false, c.handleError(err, resp, \"GetPullRequestMergeable\")\n   414|\t}\n   415|\n   416|\tc.handleRateLimit(resp)\n   417|\n   418|\tif pr.Mergeable == nil {\n   419|\t\t// Status is unknown (GitHub is still computing)\n   420|\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"mergeable status is unknown\")\n   421|\t}\n   422|\n   423|\treturn *pr.Mergeable, nil\n   424|}\n   425|\n   426|// CheckCollaboratorPermission checks if a user is a collaborator on the repository\n   427|// Returns true if the user is a collaborator (204 response), false otherwise\n   428|//\n   429|// Note: This method only checks for explicit collaborators and does not include\n   430|// repository owners or organization team members with write/admin access.\n   431|// For a more comprehensive check that includes owners and team members,\n   432|// use CheckWritePermission instead.\n   433|func (c *Client) CheckCollaboratorPermission(ctx context.Context, owner, repo, username string) (bool, error) {\n   434|\tc.logger.Info(\"Checking GitHub collaborator permission\",\n</search_result>\n<search_result path=\"specs/001-github-agent-automation/contracts/github-webhooks.md\" startLine=\"185\" endLine=\"291\">\n   185|**Purpose**: Detect Codex approval for auto-merge\n   186|\n   187|**Webhook Payload**:\n   188|\n   189|```json\n   190|{\n   191|  \"action\": \"submitted\",\n   192|  \"review\": {\n   193|    \"id\": 111222,\n   194|    \"body\": \"Codex Review: Didn't find any major issues.\",\n   195|    \"user\": {\n   196|      \"login\": \"codex-bot\"\n   197|    },\n   198|    \"state\": \"approved\"\n   199|  },\n   200|  \"pull_request\": {\n   201|    \"number\": 101\n   202|  },\n   203|  \"repository\": {\n   204|    \"full_name\": \"octocat/hello-world\"\n   205|  }\n   206|}\n   207|```\n   208|\n   209|**Processing**:\n   210|\n   211|1. Check if `review.user.login` is Codex bot\n   212|2. Parse `review.body` for approval pattern:\n   213|   - Regex: `/didn't find.*major issues/i`\n   214|   - Or exact: \"Codex Review: Didn't find any major issues.\"\n   215|3. Create ReviewFeedback record with `approval_detected: true`\n   216|4. Re-evaluate merge conditions (MergeConditionChecker)\n   217|5. If all conditions met, call AutoMergeService\n   218|6. Log to AuditLog\n   219|\n   220|---\n   221|\n   222|### 5. pull_request_review_comment\n   223|\n   224|Triggered when a comment is made on a PR review (inline code comments).\n   225|\n   226|**Purpose**: Detect `@codex review` requests in PR comments\n   227|\n   228|**Webhook Payload**:\n   229|\n   230|```json\n   231|{\n   232|  \"action\": \"created\",\n   233|  \"comment\": {\n   234|    \"id\": 333444,\n   235|    \"body\": \"@codex review\",\n   236|    \"user\": {\n   237|      \"login\": \"octocat\"\n   238|    }\n   239|  },\n   240|  \"pull_request\": {\n   241|    \"number\": 101\n   242|  },\n   243|  \"repository\": {\n   244|    \"full_name\": \"octocat/hello-world\"\n   245|  }\n   246|}\n   247|```\n   248|\n   249|**Processing**:\n   250|\n   251|1. Check if `comment.body` contains `@codex review`\n   252|2. Verify user has permission\n   253|3. Call CodexReviewService to request review\n   254|4. Create ReviewFeedback record with status=requested\n   255|5. Log to AuditLog\n   256|\n   257|---\n   258|\n   259|### 6. check_suite (FR-014)\n   260|\n   261|Triggered when a CI check suite is completed.\n   262|\n   263|**Purpose**: Detect CI pass/fail for auto-merge and AI retry\n   264|\n   265|**Actions Subscribed**: `completed`\n   266|\n   267|**Webhook Payload**:\n   268|\n   269|```json\n   270|{\n   271|  \"action\": \"completed\",\n   272|  \"check_suite\": {\n   273|    \"id\": 555666,\n   274|    \"status\": \"completed\",\n   275|    \"conclusion\": \"success\",\n   276|    \"head_branch\": \"feature/issue-42\",\n   277|    \"head_sha\": \"abc123def456\",\n   278|    \"pull_requests\": [\n   279|      {\n   280|        \"number\": 101\n   281|      }\n   282|    ]\n   283|  },\n   284|  \"repository\": {\n   285|    \"full_name\": \"octocat/hello-world\"\n   286|  }\n   287|}\n   288|```\n   289|\n   290|**Conclusion Values**:\n   291|- `success`: All checks passed\n</search_result>\n\n<search_result path=\"specs/001-github-agent-automation/spec.md\" startLine=\"59\" endLine=\"107\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"specs/001-github-agent-automation/spec.md\" startLine=\"152\" endLine=\"180\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"internal/repositories/pull_request.go\" startLine=\"63\" endLine=\"92\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"specs/001-github-agent-automation/spec.md\" startLine=\"141\" endLine=\"155\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"internal/models/pull_request.go\" endLine=\"29\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"internal/clients/discord.go\" startLine=\"414\" endLine=\"480\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"specs/001-github-agent-automation/spec.md\" startLine=\"133\" endLine=\"145\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"specs/001-github-agent-automation/plan.md\" startLine=\"192\" endLine=\"229\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"migrations/000001_init.sql\" endLine=\"46\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"specs/001-github-agent-automation/spec.md\" startLine=\"217\" endLine=\"252\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"specs/001-github-agent-automation/spec.md\" startLine=\"103\" endLine=\"136\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"internal/webhooks/handlers/issue_comment.go\" startLine=\"269\" endLine=\"327\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"specs/001-github-agent-automation/quickstart.md\" startLine=\"479\" endLine=\"567\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"internal/webhooks/handlers/pr_review_comment.go\" startLine=\"153\" endLine=\"213\"></search_result>\n<search_result path=\"internal/repositories/agent_run.go\" startLine=\"198\" endLine=\"247\"></search_result>","codeResults":[{"codeBlock":{"relativeWorkspacePath":"specs/001-github-agent-automation/data-model.md","range":{"startPosition":{"line":344,"column":0},"endPosition":{"line":394,"column":0}},"contents":"- Send Discord notification (embed with error history)\n- Stop auto-retry loop\n- Manual re-trigger available via CLI with `--reset-count` flag\n\n### PullRequest Merge Conditions (Definition of Done)\n\nA PR can be auto-merged when ALL of the following are true:\n\n1. **CI Success**: All CIStatus records have conclusion=success\n2. **Codex Approval**: At least one ReviewFeedback has approval_detected=true\n3. **No Conflicts**: PullRequest.mergeable=true (from GitHub API)\n4. **Status**: PullRequest.status=open\n\n**Checking Strategy**:\n- Re-evaluate on every check_suite.completed webhook\n- Re-evaluate on every Codex review comment webhook\n- Use MergeConditionChecker service to validate all conditions\n- Call AutoMergeService if conditions met\n\n### BlockerGraph Dependencies\n\n**Dependency Resolution**:\n- Task Y is blocked if EXISTS BlockerGraphEdges WHERE task_id=Y AND depends_on_task_id IN (open Issues)\n- Task Y is unblocked when ALL dependencies have Issue.state=closed\n- On Issue close: query BlockerGraphEdges to find newly unblocked tasks\n- Trigger new AgentRun for each unblocked task\n\n**Cycle Detection**:\n- Run DFS before starting execution\n- If cycle detected: log warning, add to AuditLog, notify in GitHub comment\n- Do NOT block execution (spec allows human resolution)\n\n## 制約情報（MySQL/GORM）\n\n### Unique Constraints\n- Issue: UNIQUE(repo, number)\n- PullRequest: UNIQUE(repo, number)\n- AgentRun: UNIQUE(idempotency_key)\n- CIStatus: UNIQUE(pr_id, check_suite_id, check_run_id)\n- BlockerGraphEdges: PRIMARY KEY(task_id, depends_on_task_id)\n\n### Foreign Key Constraints\n- AgentRun.issue_id → Issue.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n- AgentRun.pr_id → PullRequest.id (ON DELETE SET NULL)\n- PullRequest.issue_id → Issue.id (ON DELETE SET NULL)\n- ReviewFeedback.pr_id → PullRequest.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n- CIStatus.pr_id → PullRequest.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n- BlockerGraphEdges.task_id → Issue.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n- BlockerGraphEdges.depends_on_task_id → Issue.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)","signatures":{"ranges":[]},"detailedLines":[{"text":"- Send Discord notification (embed with error history)","lineNumber":345,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- Stop auto-retry loop","lineNumber":346,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- Manual re-trigger available via CLI with `--reset-count` flag","lineNumber":347,"isSignature":false},{"text":"","lineNumber":348,"isSignature":false},{"text":"### PullRequest Merge Conditions (Definition of Done)","lineNumber":349,"isSignature":false},{"text":"","lineNumber":350,"isSignature":false},{"text":"A PR can be auto-merged when ALL of the following are true:","lineNumber":351,"isSignature":false},{"text":"","lineNumber":352,"isSignature":false},{"text":"1. **CI Success**: All CIStatus records have conclusion=success","lineNumber":353,"isSignature":false},{"text":"2. **Codex Approval**: At least one ReviewFeedback has approval_detected=true","lineNumber":354,"isSignature":false},{"text":"3. **No Conflicts**: PullRequest.mergeable=true (from GitHub API)","lineNumber":355,"isSignature":false},{"text":"4. **Status**: PullRequest.status=open","lineNumber":356,"isSignature":false},{"text":"","lineNumber":357,"isSignature":false},{"text":"**Checking Strategy**:","lineNumber":358,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- Re-evaluate on every check_suite.completed webhook","lineNumber":359,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- Re-evaluate on every Codex review comment webhook","lineNumber":360,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- Use MergeConditionChecker service to validate all conditions","lineNumber":361,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- Call AutoMergeService if conditions met","lineNumber":362,"isSignature":false},{"text":"","lineNumber":363,"isSignature":false},{"text":"### BlockerGraph Dependencies","lineNumber":364,"isSignature":false},{"text":"","lineNumber":365,"isSignature":false},{"text":"**Dependency Resolution**:","lineNumber":366,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- Task Y is blocked if EXISTS BlockerGraphEdges WHERE task_id=Y AND depends_on_task_id IN (open Issues)","lineNumber":367,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- Task Y is unblocked when ALL dependencies have Issue.state=closed","lineNumber":368,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- On Issue close: query BlockerGraphEdges to find newly unblocked tasks","lineNumber":369,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- Trigger new AgentRun for each unblocked task","lineNumber":370,"isSignature":false},{"text":"","lineNumber":371,"isSignature":false},{"text":"**Cycle Detection**:","lineNumber":372,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- Run DFS before starting execution","lineNumber":373,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- If cycle detected: log warning, add to AuditLog, notify in GitHub comment","lineNumber":374,"isSignature":false},{"text":"- Do NOT block execution (spec allows human resolution)","lineNumber":375,"isSignature":false},{"text":"","lineNumber":376,"isSignature":false},{"text":"## 制約情報（MySQL/GORM）","lineNumber":377,"isSignature":false},{"text":"","lineNumber":378,"isSignature":false},{"text":"### Unique Constraints","lineNumber":379,"isSignature":false},{"text":"